# 0081-redesign-ipad-sidebar-hero-inspector.patch -- the iPad layout of the redesign (the owner's prototype target/agent-work/design/project/iPad.dc.html, 1180 x 820 landscape): a left
# sidebar instead of the tab bar, the Library as a hero of the selected game above a 4-column grid, the game's page in a right INSPECTOR instead of the bottom sheet, Build and Settings in
# two columns. A compact width keeps 0080's iPhone layout exactly.
# Applies after 0080. UNTESTED ON AN IPAD, IN THE SIMULATOR AND ON A PHONE: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below). Kept apart from 0080 at the coordinator's suggestion.
#
# WHEN: PadLayout.Applies (GameAppPad.cs, pure): a REGULAR horizontal size class AND at least 820 pt of safe-area width (0062's WideFrom), never in an exported player. Decided in
#   ApplyAdaptiveLayout after every layout (a rotation, Split View, Slide Over, a Stage Manager resize switch it); the change (SetPadWide) is made once per change. With it 0062's Settings split
#   (Settings in a left column, its pages on the right) is not used: Settings has the whole width beside the sidebar and its pages open over it with their back button.
# WHAT (GameAppPadUi.cs, new; small hooks in GameAppLibrary.cs, GameAppRedesignUi.cs, GameAppShelf.cs):
#   * the sidebar (250 pt, #121217, a hairline edge): the iBuilder mark, Library / Build / Settings (44 pt rows, the lit one an ink capsule, with their counts: the games; "1 building · 2
#     queued"; the log's errors), SOURCES (the cached cloud sources and their game files, each -> the Cloud page), a storage card at the bottom (0064's bar, the free space). The capsule tab bar
#     is hidden and the pages reach the bottom (their constraint to the bar is swapped for one to the safe area); every page starts beside the sidebar.
#   * Library: the hero (a 250 pt cover, the status pill, the title 34 pt, the meta line, the state's buttons of 0080 at 52 pt, the round settings button, the get-task-allow line) above "All games",
#     a grid of 4 columns, 3 while the inspector is open; a tap on a card selects the hero's game (the hero's settings button or its cover opens the inspector); touch and hold is 0080's menu,
#     anchored with the grid's real column count; the carousel and its toggle are not shown; the glow follows the hero's game.
#   * the inspector (360 pt on the right): ShowGameSheet's own page (0080's sheet) as a child navigation controller instead of a presented sheet; its actions close it first (as the sheet closed
#     itself), its Close button closes it; the library's page makes room for it.
#   * Build: the "Now building" card on the left, the import card, the queue, the shader preparation, the filter and the game lists on the right. Settings: the four tiles in one row, then the
#     build settings and the sources on the left, the storage card, the diagnostics and the footer on the right. On a phone both keep 0080's order (they are re-stacked on a change).
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-21, M1 Pro)
#   * scripts/check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree (diff -r).
#   * Compile (the same device project, GameAppPad.cs and GameAppPadUi.cs added): `dotnet build gameapp.csproj -c Release -r ios-arm64 -t:Compile`: 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and
#     code as the 0079 and 0080 trees. "layout: iPad (sidebar, hero, inspector)" and "All games" are in the compiled GameApp.dll.
#   * Host harness (target/agent-work/redesign/harness81: 0080's harness compiled with PAD81 and GameAppPad.cs over this tree): 131 of 131 checks (0080's 118 and 13 for this patch: when it
#     applies, the columns, the sizes, the counts, the menu's anchoring in 4 columns, the wiring read from the UIKit files); 11 of 11 mutations of this patch are killed (mutate81.py).
#
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on an iPad: the sidebar's and the inspector's look, the switch between the layouts on a rotation or a resize, a child navigation controller's pushed settings page in
#   a 360 pt panel (its own "Done" button is a sheet's and does nothing there: its back button returns), the hero's sizes in a narrow regular window (820 pt), VoiceOver order. The prototype's
#   certificate chip in the library header and the Build column's list of the + menu entries are not reproduced (the certificate is Settings' tile, the + menu is the Build header's).
#
# NEW UI STRINGS: "iBuilder" (the sidebar's mark), "All games", the counts " building", " queued", " error(s)"; log lines "layout: iPad (sidebar, hero, inspector)", "layout: compact (the iPhone's)".
